v("STAR.Gaia_RV","CORRECTED","RV 10.486 +- 0.221 km/s; rv_nb_transits 33; rv_chisq_pvalue 4.06e-5; rv_renormalised_gof 2.999; rv_amplitude_robust 3.22 km/s; not RV-variable under the Gaia DR3 rule (p<0.01 AND gof>4 AND N>=10; fails gof only). Context: the gof is at the 84th percentile of all 772 comparable stars, but at the 91st percentile among apparently single stars (n=543) and the 96.6th among RUWE<1.4 stars (n=589); only 3.4% of RUWE<1.4 comparable stars have p <= 4.06e-5. The RV epoch scatter is therefore elevated relative to well-behaved single stars, not 'mildly above average'.","Values and the official rule are right (Gaia DR3 gaia_source data model, re-fetched 2026-09-25 ~15:55 UTC: 'rv_chisq_pvalue <0.01 and rv_renormalised_gof >4 and rv_nb_transits >=10'). But the reconciler's interpretation ('mildly above average, not anomalous') uses a binary-rich reference population, the very argument it rejected for RUWE. Against apparently single stars the scatter is in the top 4-9%.","verify/v01_ruwe_rv_check.json single.gof_pct_below, all_ruwe_lt1p4.gof_pct_below, frac_p_le_target; 06_stellar/data/gaia_dr3_source.ecsv rv_*")
