v("STAR.rotation","CORRECTED","No rotation period is established. In the project's own Sector 32 SPOC 2-min PDCSAP light curve (transits masked, 30-min bins), the strongest Lomb-Scargle peak (0.5-20 d) is at 7.97 d with semi-amplitude ~550 ppm (~1.1 mmag peak-to-peak; ~3 cycles in 25.8 d), matching the catalogue values (Gao+2025 8.18 d, Schmitt+2026 8.11 d, Wang+2025 7.98 d, TESS-SVC 7.98 +- 0.79 d). The same period is absent in Sector 6 TESS-SPOC PDCSAP (<~0.1-0.2 mmag; top peak 12.5 d, 170 ppm), and SAP/QLP light curves are dominated by systematics. Ground surveys (KELT/ASAS-3/ASAS-SN) are null but insensitive below ~1.8 mmag. The ~8 d signal is single-sector and unconfirmed (stellar rotation or PDC residual).","The reconciler's statement that the ~8 d signal is 'not recovered in the project photometry' is false: it is the dominant periodicity of S32 PDCSAP. The audit s15 check used SAP only, which is dominated by sector-length trends. The conclusion 'no rotation period' still holds because the signal is absent in S6 PDCSAP and covers only ~3 cycles.","verify/v02_s32_rotation_ls.json PDCSAP_FLUX (top_period_d 7.970, top_semi_amp_ppm 554); verify/v03_other_sectors_ls.json (S6 PDCSAP top 12.51 d, 169 ppm; 7.5-8.7 d band 70 ppm); input deep_followup_tic4206066/lc/tess2020324010417-s0032-0000000004206066-0200-s_lc.fits")
v("STAR.xray","CONFIRMED","","Raw eRASS1 row: posErr 5.363, DetLike0 8.04, MLcts1 4.49, MLExp1 124.1 s, MLFlux1 3.3686e-14 (+2.02/-1.44e-14). Wright+2011 coefficients checked in the paper text (log RXsat -3.13, Ro_sat 0.13, beta -2.18 / -2.70, ~0.3 dex rms, Eq. 11, Table 2 V-Ks 3.36-3.68 log tau 1.67 / 1.49). L_X 5.10e27 recomputed by hand.","archival_extra_tic4206066/spectra_activity/raw/vizier_5as/J_A+A_682_A34_erass1-m.csv; _work/T6_star/out/t6_03_xray_rossby.json; verify/wright2011_text.txt L370-374, L819-857, L968")
v("STAR.chromosphere","CONFIRMED","","Halpha absorption +0.606/+0.628/+0.587 A (own MRS measurement, S/N 59-85) and ESP-ELS -0.0841 +- 0.0068 nm with flag 1 (model -0.186 nm subtracted) confirmed; Gaia AP data model re-fetched (unit nm; flag 1 = model subtracted for Teff < 5000 K). Caveat: the saved Ren+2026 ReadMe does not document the EW sign; EW8542 -1.29 and EW8662 -1.83 A have photospheric-absorption magnitudes under a negative=absorption convention, but EW8498 is +0.50, so 'Ca II IRT in absorption' is an inference, not a documented fact.","spectra_activity/REPORT.md L55-L57, L79-L80; opus55 00_data/catalogs/gaiadr3_astrophysical_parameters_target.ecsv (unit nm, flag 1, model -0.185936); spectra_activity/raw/vizier_5as/J_ApJS_282_29_table1.csv; raw/readme/J_ApJS_282_29.txt")
v("STAR.activity_status","CORRECTED","No rotation period is established (a 7.97 d, ~0.55 mmag semi-amplitude modulation appears only in Sector 32 PDCSAP and not in Sector 6). The star is chromospherically quiet (Halpha in absorption, no TESS flares) and has a marginal eRASS1 X-ray detection with log L_X/L_bol ~ -4.8 (unsaturated), which under Wright+2011 suggests P ~ 13-50 d.","'No rotation period is detected' and 'unconfirmed catalogue periodicity' understate that the project's own S32 PDCSAP light curve shows the ~8 d signal. The corrected wording keeps the conclusion (no established period).","verify/v02_s32_rotation_ls.json; verify/v03_other_sectors_ls.json; _work/T6_star/out/t6_03_xray_rossby.json")
